{
    "2024.acl-long.751_s01": "The proposed method has been extensively studied for moral reasoning.",
    "2024.acl-long.751_s02": "The extension of reasoning using SKIG in domains like negotiation which require multi-stakeholder alignment are yet to be studied.",
    "2024.acl-long.751_s03": "Also, the reasoning path could generate harmful responses for scenarios rarely, strategies to address such responses need to be improved."
}

{
    "2024.c3nlp-1.9_s01": "The main limitation of this project is the lack of direct language community involvement.",
    "2024.c3nlp-1.9_s02": "This paper attempts to address cross-cultural considerations by referring to research that encourages and demonstrates involvement by and feedback from a variety of language communities, but subsequent research should include consultation with multiple language communities."
}

{
    "2025.acl-long.2_s01": "The backbone of GraphNarrator is based on LLMs, which may be more costly to do inference than saliency-based explanation methods.",
    "2025.acl-long.2_s02": "For long documents although KV-cache can bring significant improvements for inference, we still find for a few extremely large subgraphs, the inference time could exceed 2 mins."
}

{
    "2024.findings-acl.931_s01": "While emotion2vec provides a universal emotion representation, it requires training separate downstream models when testing different emotionrelated tasks.",
    "2024.findings-acl.931_s02": "In addition, whether speaker information is removed exists not explored, which is critical for training emotional TTS systems with the emotion2vec representations."
}

{
    "2022.emnlp-main.99_s01": "Although our work has revealed the vulnerability of model extraction through a lens of privacy leakage, we have not proposed an effective enough defense approach for AIA.",
    "2022.emnlp-main.99_s02": "Thus, we encourage the community to investigate this direction to mitigate the adverse social impacts caused by this attack."
}

{
    "2022.findings-emnlp.98_s01": "The main limitation of our model is that the approximate decoding schemes introduce significant computational overhead in comparison to the direct model and CTRL, which amounts to a factor of up to 10 for online decoding with a large beam size using a not yet fully optimized implementation.",
    "2022.findings-emnlp.98_s02": "Furthermore, decoding is a lot more complex and the scaling factors need to be tuned which implies significant additional computations that are necessary and results in a larger carbon footprint.",
    "2022.findings-emnlp.98_s03": "In addition, our noisy channel model has a significantly higher number of parameters than the baseline model.",
    "2022.findings-emnlp.98_s04": "Finally, we mainly rely on automatic metrics to assess the faithfulness of the proposed approaches and leave out a broader evaluation of the general quality of generated responses but for a small-scale qualitative study cf. Section 6.5."
}

{
    "2024.acl-long.118_s01": "Although our measurement disagreement maximization model is demonstrated effective, it may have two limitations.",
    "2024.acl-long.118_s02": "First, ADM relies on a twostage pre-training process to obtain an initialized ID classifier and outlier detector, which guarantees the effectiveness of the min-max optimization.",
    "2024.acl-long.118_s03": "Second, ADM requires the proposed abnormal-example detection and measurement calibration approach to guarantee the correct optimization direction."
}

{
    "2024.findings-acl.434_s01": "Despite the potential advantages of Partialformer in terms of parameter utilization \n and performance within a limited parameter budget, it is important to note that the existing conclusions regarding i\n ts effectiveness have not been thoroughly examined in the context of large-scale datasets \n and a higher number of parameters.",
    "2024.findings-acl.434_s02": "Further research is needed to validate the claims and assess the scalability of Partialformer in more challenging scenarios."
}

{
    "2021.findings-emnlp.408_s01": "Limitations Modeling the social networks with GAT is affected by several factors.",
    "2021.findings-emnlp.408_s02": "First, the low graph density, as the original dataset wasn't col-lected by following relationships between users, hence many users across different conversation threads are not related to each other.",
    "2021.findings-emnlp.408_s03": "Second, the homophily degree is only 32%, users with sarcastic tendency have few connections among them."
}

{
    "2022.acl-long.18_s01": "‚Äö√Ñ¬¢ Our approach is expected to improve crosslingual transfer from HRL to LRL only when the HRL and LRL are related linguistically since it relies on the presence of lexically overlapping tokens",
    "2022.acl-long.18_s02": "‚Äö√Ñ¬¢ It requires the transliteration of LRL data to the script of its related HRL if LRL does not have the same script."
}

{
    "2024.findings-acl.929_s01": "While token alignment works in principles on any tokenizer, it may require additional attention to details to implement, especially with tokenizers that are not lossless which could make the token alignment process tricky.",
    "2024.findings-acl.929_s02": "The latency addition due to token alignment is generally small for long generation, but can be a larger portion of overall budget if the generation is short."
}

{
    "2024.nlp4convai-1.3_s01": "Regarding the participants of our user study, all of them are internal employees of a giant tech company, the majority of whom are highly educated (60% hold a master‚Äö√Ñ√∂‚àö√ë‚àö¬•s or doctoral degree).",
    "2024.nlp4convai-1.3_s02": "However, they show various experiences with chatbots, not correlated with educational degree.",
    "2024.nlp4convai-1.3_s03": "Some of them are bilingual, while others are not native English speakers.",
    "2024.nlp4convai-1.3_s04": "Furthermore, since we assume a traveling situation, the conversational scenario was not challenging, even for non-native speakers."
}

{
    "2024.findings-acl.612_s01": "Since we used only limited human-related nouns to extract knowledge from the existing knowledge base, the knowledge is not comprehensive.",
    "2024.findings-acl.612_s02": "This causes a weaker control in certain bias categories.",
    "2024.findings-acl.612_s03": "Developing a method for acquiring more comprehensive structured knowledge or data augmentation will be the focus of future research."
}

{
    "2024.acl-short.64_s01": "The DUAL-REFLECT framework enhances the reflective capabilities of LLMs in translation tasks by leveraging the duality nature of translation but has several limitations.",
    "2024.acl-short.64_s02": "Firstly, models with stronger reflective capabilities will obtain better feedback, thereby enhancing more performance.",
    "2024.acl-short.64_s03": "Additionally, since our method requires multiple steps, it necessitates a significant amount of computational resources."
}

{
    "2025.findings-emnlp.142_s01": "The limitations of our work can be summarized as follows.",
    "2025.findings-emnlp.142_s02": "While the model demonstrated enhancements on the particular datasets ASAP and ASASP++, it has not been tested on other datasets and other languages.",
    "2025.findings-emnlp.142_s03": "For cross-prompt essay scoring, learning generalizable essay representations helps enhance the model's ability to score across different prompts.",
    "2025.findings-emnlp.142_s04": "Therefore, further exploration of methods that enhance the generalizability of essay representations could further improve the model's cross-prompt scoring capabilities."
}

{
    "2024.acl-demos.34_s01": "The current demonstration uses external LLMbased APIs but can be adapted to open source LLM models.",
    "2024.acl-demos.34_s02": "‚Äö√Ñ√∂The LLM-based inferences require a critical supporting quantitative evaluation and hallucinations are possible.",
    "2024.acl-demos.34_s03": "The current workflow is motivated by a hypothesis generation process, which is fully human supervised and does not have direct clinical applications."
}

{
    "2024.findings-acl.884_s01": "Despite that DEmO achieves impressive results, it still faces the following limitations:",
    "2024.findings-acl.884_s02": "(1) Our framework is limited by the lack of label information, particularly on imbalanced datasets",
    "2024.findings-acl.884_s03": "(2) The metrics of content-free entropy and influence are designed for classification tasks.",
    "2024.findings-acl.884_s04": "More reasonable metrics rather than naive operation on the the first token are supposed to be explored."
}

{
    "2024.acl-long.569_s01": "The prompt learning-based approach heavily relies on the capabilities of LLMs, and in scenarios involving multiple rounds of dialogue, the cost of reasoning becomes significantly high.",
    "2024.acl-long.569_s02": "Additionally, it is impractical to adjust the output of LLM when invoking LLM APIs.",
    "2024.acl-long.569_s03": "Therefore, this paper proposes a collaborative human-machine annotation method to mitigate this issue."
}

{
    "2024.sighan-1.4_s01": "The current exploration, while demonstrating promising advancements, has areas for potential enhancement.",
    "2024.sighan-1.4_s02": "Firstly, the study‚Äö√Ñ√∂‚àö√ë‚àö¬•s focus on a limited number of languages may not fully capture the breadth of linguistic diversity, potentially affecting the model‚Äö√Ñ√∂‚àö√ë‚àö¬•s adaptability in multilingual scenarios.",
    "2024.sighan-1.4_s03": "Secondly, variations in data quality could impact the robustness of the model‚Äö√Ñ√∂‚àö√ë‚àö¬•s generalization capabilities."
}

{
    "2024.wassa-1.22_s01": "One particular limitation of our work is the usage of two specific aspects of style: Politeness and Negotiation.",
    "2024.wassa-1.22_s02": "To ensure concise insights we limited the experiments to these two aspects since they pertain the most to the task specific dataset we used (CraigslistBargains).",
    "2024.wassa-1.22_s03": "We believe the results observed for these two aspects should translate to other facets of style on other datasets and we hope to address this by expanding on these experiments in our future work."
}

{
    "2024.textgraphs-1.13_s01": "The effectiveness of CoT-Questioning depends on the model used.",
    "2024.textgraphs-1.13_s02": "As observed from the results, larger models excel at simplifying questions.",
    "2024.textgraphs-1.13_s03": "Additionally, the accuracy of the final answers depends on the data the model has been trained with, so it can produce outdated answers.",
    "2024.textgraphs-1.13_s04": "Better methods to incorporate the information present in KGs could help address this problem."
}

{
    "2024.findings-acl.23_s01": "In this study, we do not intend to exhaust every possible text representation, image representation of tables, or every possible LLM.",
    "2024.findings-acl.23_s02": "Moreover, we do not have access to the closed-source LLMs behind their API.",
    "2024.findings-acl.23_s03": "Instead, we designed our experiments to try to explore the research questions we raised in this paper.",
    "2024.findings-acl.23_s04": "We hope our findings and insights in this paper can inspire future research on table-related tasks."
}

{
    "2022.emnlp-main.310_s01": "The major limitation of MetaLogic is that we cannot annotate a large enough dataset for data-driven methods.",
    "2022.emnlp-main.310_s02": "However, considering that humans could learn to conduct logical reasoning after seeing a few examples, we argue that it is meaningful to investigate whether machines can learn the same level of reasoning capability with limited data."
}

{
    "2020.emnlp-main.110_s01": "Limitations.",
    "2020.emnlp-main.110_s02": "This work does not capture all methods that have been proposed for assessing political approval but focuses on those that have been popular in the past or are exemplary for different types of methods (untargeted sentiment, targeted sentiment, and stance).",
    "2020.emnlp-main.110_s03": "Second, we only consider approval towards named entities, which we find is already a difficult task, especially for indirect stances.",
    "2020.emnlp-main.110_s04": "In the future, we hope to explore abstract topics like 'immigration' where differentiating between direct and indirect stance is non-trivial and ensemble models that combine the strengths of multiple methods."
}

{
    "2024.acl-long.666_s01": "STRUCT-IOU is designed to evaluate constituency parse trees over continuous spoken word boundaries, and is not directly applicable to evaluate other types of parses, such as dependency parse trees;",
    "2024.acl-long.666_s02": "however, it may be extended to evaluate other types of parse trees by modifying the alignment constraints.",
    "2024.acl-long.666_s03": "We leave the extension of STRUCTIOU to other types of parses as future work.",
    "2024.acl-long.666_s04": "We do not foresee any risk associated with the use of STRUCT-IOU beyond the inherent minimal risks encountered in computer science research."
}

{
    "2024.emnlp-main.1235_s01": "This work introduces a new mechanism by which to approach the the shortcomings of LLM alignment, and as such does not encompass every avenue of exploration.",
    "2024.emnlp-main.1235_s02": "Future work could explore possible defense mechanisms against IRIS and investigate the effects of iteratively applying the Rate+Enhance step, which we only experiment with once in this study.",
    "2024.emnlp-main.1235_s03": "Additionally, the prompt templates used in IRIS have only one format, which may be easy to detect.",
    "2024.emnlp-main.1235_s04": "Future research could explore methods for automatically generating these templates to improve the robustness of the approach."
}

{
    "2020.acl-main.243_s01": "Limitations Given the promise of PR as a technique for inducing control states, it is worth noting some of the current limitations to our specific application of the method.",
    "2020.acl-main.243_s02": "Currently, we use simple rules which do not generalize well to paraphrase.",
    "2020.acl-main.243_s03": "Our weak supervision relies on direct overlap to align states and fails on aligning phrases like less then 10 dollars that are expressed as cheap.",
    "2020.acl-main.243_s04": "Additionally, while at test time, our method is comparable to a standard decoder model, it does require slightly longer to train due to both the dynamic program and the requirement to compute multiple samples."
}

{
    "2024.sighan-1.11_s01": "Although our proposed system enhances the quality of dimensional intensity prediction, there are still several limitations.",
    "2024.sighan-1.11_s02": "First, we have only validated the effectiveness of the joint learning strategy for intensity prediction and have not tested it for fine-grained aspect extraction.",
    "2024.sighan-1.11_s03": "Second, our current approach uses traditional PLMs as backbones.",
    "2024.sighan-1.11_s04": "In the future, we plan to explore the use of largescale PLMs, such as ChatGPT and LLaMA, for dimABSA tasks."
}

{
    "2024.findings-acl.668_s01": "Since our method incorporates a learnable module for enhancing sentence embeddings, MixSP‚Äö√Ñ√∂‚àö√ë‚àö¬•s parameter increases from 110 million to 145 million parameters, as shown in Table 6.",
    "2024.findings-acl.668_s02": "In addition, the training time and memory usage of our method are also higher than competitor methods.",
    "2024.findings-acl.668_s03": "However, regarding performance, our method outperforms competitors in all cases."
}

{
    "2023.acl-short.96_s01": "Although FPT shows better control ability, there are two points that need to be improved in the future.",
    "2023.acl-short.96_s02": "First, as in Gu et al. (2022), we need to select hyperparameter ≈í¬± to balance between the control ability and fluency in generated texts.",
    "2023.acl-short.96_s03": "Second, as shown in Table 5, although the time cost of FPT is lower than that of GeDi, it is higher than those of other prefix tuning-based methods and grows approximately linearly by a factor of 2 ‚àö√≥ number of attributes."
}

{
    "2024.findings-acl.227_s01": "Our work has limitations in terms of creating a connecting context ‚Äö√Ñ√∂‚àö√ë‚àö√Ü such a context will only be created if there is some path between two entities in Wikidata.",
    "2024.findings-acl.227_s02": "We plan to overcome this limitation by incorporating other external knowledge bases for creating context.",
    "2024.findings-acl.227_s03": "With the increase in the number of text paths and mentioned entities, the GPU memory consumption increases, and the speed decreases."
}

{
    "2024.findings-acl.44_s01": "While the proposed method effectively mitigates catastrophic forgetting to some extent, its reliance on the predictions of old models for preserving existing knowledge can result in accumulated prediction errors, which may lead to poor model performance in more incremental steps.",
    "2024.findings-acl.44_s02": "Moreover, the current method does not thoroughly explore the relationship between the penalty effect and the dataset, leaving potential avenues for future research."
}

title:
NU at WASSA 2024 Empathy and Personality Shared Task: 
 Enhancing Personality Predictions with Knowledge Graphs; 
 A Graphical Neural Network and LightGBM Ensemble Approach

segmented_text:
{
    "2024.wassa-1.36_s01": "The process of extracting meaningful features from text using BERT and constructing knowledge graphs requires substantial computational resources.",
    "2024.wassa-1.36_s02": "Additionally, the quality of the extracted features can vary depending on the preprocessing and entity extraction methods used, potentially impacting the model‚Äö√Ñ√∂‚àö√ë‚àö¬•s performance."
}

{
    "2024.findings-acl.442_s01": "Given the diverse nature of KG-related tasks spanning multiple domains and requiring a broad range of capabilities, the implementation of a multi-agent system is promising to significantly enhance task performance.",
    "2024.findings-acl.442_s02": "We leave the integration of our observation mechanism with multi-agent system to future work."
}

{
    "2024.findings-acl.922_s01": "This work is limited to enhancing the understanding of the hidden mechanisms of Transformerbased CLMs.",
    "2024.findings-acl.922_s02": "More effort can be made by inspiration from these understandings to improve existing models and propose more advanced algorithms.",
    "2024.findings-acl.922_s03": "Our current study verifies our discovered mechanisms of Transformer-based CLMs on limited models and datasets.",
    "2024.findings-acl.922_s04": "It is interesting to study these mechanisms in more diverse scenarios."
}

{
    "2024.findings-acl.857_s01": "While we cover three low-resource languages,",
    "2024.findings-acl.857_s02": "many others like Bajjika, Surajpuri, and Maithili, which share geographical boundaries with our languages of interest, have not been included.",
    "2024.findings-acl.857_s03": "Due to the smaller size of our dataset compared to larger POS datasets, we do not have a lot of diversity across domains.",
    "2024.findings-acl.857_s04": "We note that the POS dataset and the observations in this work may not be applicable to all domains, such as speech transcripts or conversational data."
}

{
    "2024.findings-acl.248_s01": "In this paper, we propose the Position-oriented Prompt-tuning (POP-CEE) model to solve the CEE task in an end-to-end manner.",
    "2024.findings-acl.248_s02": "However, prompts and constraints are somewhat empirically designed, and an automated approach is necessary.",
    "2024.findings-acl.248_s03": "In addition, our current approach is based on RoBERTabase, and we have not yet verified its effectiveness on generative large language models.",
    "2024.findings-acl.248_s04": "Future research will focus on addressing these limitations and exploring the potential of generative models."
}

{
    "2024.privatenlp-1.17_s01": "Our experiments were mainly conducted on models up to 8B and did not include testing on larger opensource models or closed-source models.",
    "2024.privatenlp-1.17_s02": "The effectiveness of our RLTA framework on these larger and potentially more complex models remains unverified, which may limit the generalizability of our results.",
    "2024.privatenlp-1.17_s03": "Future studies should aim to apply and validate our method across a broader spectrum of LLMs to fully understand its potential and limitations in real-world scenarios."
}

{
    "2023.findings-emnlp.498_s01": "Due to the computation constraints, we were not able to experiment with our framework on more NLP tasks with more languages, which will be supplemented in the future.",
    "2023.findings-emnlp.498_s02": "The syntactic difference is a key factor affecting cross-lingual, and syntactic distance can help to understand or quantify the transfer differences.",
    "2023.findings-emnlp.498_s03": "Our framework with SDMM is a simple attempt to use syntactic distance metrics to construct meta-task and reduce the language gap in cross-lingual transfer learning.",
    "2023.findings-emnlp.498_s04": "More work needs to be done on syntactic differences and syntactic distance metrics."
}

{
    "2024.findings-acl.3_s01": "Although we pay efforts to design an efficient FPasym-based inference system in Section 3, it still incurs inference overhead compared with INT4/NF4-sym-based system shown in Section 4.",
    "2024.findings-acl.3_s02": "We believe the gap can be narrowed with advanced kernel optimizations or specific hardware design, which we leave it as a future work."
}

{
    "2024.findings-acl.623_s01": "Our examination reveals prevalence of noisy samples within the LP(1) and LPapp(1) subsets of data.",
    "2024.findings-acl.623_s02": "The detection and mitigation of noisy samples are imperative to mitigate their influence on the dataset.",
    "2024.findings-acl.623_s03": "We leave this for future work."
}

{
    "2024.findings-acl.875_s01": "Limitations",
    "2024.findings-acl.875_s02": "On one hand, this work primarily focuses on large language models and can explore even larger and more diverse model structures in the future.",
    "2024.findings-acl.875_s03": "Furthermore, several other neuron importance metrics are necessary to explore.",
    "2024.findings-acl.875_s04": "On the other hand, training numerous large-scale models requires substantial computational resources, incurring high costs and resulting in significant carbon emissions."
}

{
    "2020.acl-main.263_s01": "Although we have established our methods' effectiveness at both inducing model failure and robustifying said models, we believe they could be further improved by addressing the following limitations:",
    "2020.acl-main.263_s02": "1. MORPHEUS finds the distribution of examples that are adversarial for the target model, rather than that of real L2 speaker errors, which produced some unrealistic adversarial examples.",
    "2020.acl-main.263_s03": "2. Our method of adversarial fine-tuning is analogous to curing the symptom rather than addressing the root cause since it would have to be performed for each domain-specific dataset the model is trained on.",
    "2020.acl-main.263_s04": "In future work, we intend to address these limitations by directly modeling the L2 and dialectal distributions and investigating the possibility of robustifying these models further upstream."
}

{
    "2024.findings-acl.404_s01": "We follow the task definition of Visual Voice Cloning (V2C), which focuses on generating audio only.",
    "2024.findings-acl.404_s02": "Truly solving the larger problem would require changing the video to reflect the updated audio.",
    "2024.findings-acl.404_s03": "In future, we will add this capability to better support tasks like cross-language video translation."
}

{
    "2024.acl-long.606_s01": "Our exploration is restricted to four commonly used modalities, omitting a comprehensive examination across the entire spectrum of potential modalities.",
    "2024.acl-long.606_s02": "This limitation may result in missed opportunities to identify further benefits or challenges associated with model composition.",
    "2024.acl-long.606_s03": "Additionally, our proposed approach has been tested on models of specific sizes, leaving the applicability of the mehods on larger-scale MLLMs an open question for future research."
}

{
    "2024.findings-acl.167_s01": "This study presented a comprehensive review from a technical perspective.",
    "2024.findings-acl.167_s02": "However, the current version primarily focuses on technique, lacking analysis from a medical perspective.",
    "2024.findings-acl.167_s03": "In the future, we intend to include more in-depth comparative analyses to gain a better understanding of current medical dialogues from the medical perspective."
}

{
    "2020.acl-main.454_s01": "Since CNN/DM and XSum datasets are automatically crawled, we find that there is noise in the data.",
    "2020.acl-main.454_s02": "For example, source documents can include phrases such as \"click here for the latest news\".",
    "2020.acl-main.454_s03": "We further observe that reference can carry information that is not in the source document since some of these one sentence highlights are written using additional world knowledge.",
    "2020.acl-main.454_s04": "Table 13 shows an example where the reference is unfaithful since it includes information that is not in the source (i.e. the fact that Ms. Wood's first name is Leanne and she is Plaid Cymru leader.)."
}

{
    "2024.findings-acl.616_s01": "Our evaluation data spans 20 datasets, each containing numerous testing samples, resulting in a substantial amount of data that requires significant computation time and resources.",
    "2024.findings-acl.616_s02": "As a solution, we aim to devise criteria for identifying representative data points within each dataset to expedite the evaluation process."
}

{
    "2024.c3nlp-1.4_s01": "In this study, we concentrate on mining cultural instructions from English-language corpora.",
    "2024.c3nlp-1.4_s02": "However, it is important to recognize that cultural concepts are often deeply integrated with their respective languages, including those that are primarily spoken.",
    "2024.c3nlp-1.4_s03": "Therefore, to effectively synthesize cultural concepts and instructions, adopting multilingual approaches (Liu et al., 2023; Lin et al., 2024) is essential to accommodate a broader range of cultural contexts."
}

{
    "2023.acl-short.156_s01": "One of the limitations of our survey is that it covers a limited sample space of 15 papers from EMNLP 2020 and ACL 2020.",
    "2023.acl-short.156_s02": "While a larger sample would be helpful in gathering more evidence, access to specific tracks is limited at NLP conferences, unless hosted online via a virtual or hybrid system.",
    "2023.acl-short.156_s03": "With respect to our case study, we evaluate on the ASR utterances, but with labels corresponding to the original manual transcriptions.",
    "2023.acl-short.156_s04": "For a perfect comparison, the ASR utterances would need to be re-annotated as the talk move could change based on the severity of transcription errors."
