{
    "2024.findings-acl.171_s01": "As shown in the experiments, HyperCL is more powerful in predicting entities than relations.",
    "2024.findings-acl.171_s02": "Besides the reason that the problem space of relations is usually much smaller than that of entities, this is also partially attributed to the current framework not taking into account the contrastive learning of relations.",
    "2024.findings-acl.171_s03": "In the future, we will consider extending our framework to contrastive relations as a unified architecture."
}

{
    "2024.findings-acl.20_s01": "Our ImplicitAVE dataset does not consider multivalued attributes and negative instances, i.e. \"none\" as attribute values.",
    "2024.findings-acl.20_s02": "We leave this extension as future work.",
    "2024.findings-acl.20_s03": "Due to computational resource constraints and limited budgets, we did not evaluate open MLLMs with parameters larger than 13B."
}

{
    "2021.emnlp-main.376_s01": "Limitations",
    "2021.emnlp-main.376_s02": "In our choice of languages, we wanted to ensure diversity.",
    "2021.emnlp-main.376_s03": "Nevertheless, four of the analyzed languages belong to an Indo-European family that could facilitate finding shared encoding subspace for those languages."
}

{
    "2024.findings-acl.693_s01": "The advantages of Post-Ins are likely to be more pronounced with longer text data (such as paragraph data), and we plan to explore its performance on extended text in future work.",
    "2024.findings-acl.693_s02": "The effectiveness of Post-Ins on larger scale models also warrants further investigation."
}

{
    "2025.emnlp-main.883_s01": "Our approach currently supports basic graph query operations but does not handle advanced constructs such as ORDER BY , LIMIT , UNION , or complex FILTER clauses.",
    "2025.emnlp-main.883_s02": "Incorporating these may be possible by enabling the LLM to generate additional query operators and appropriately applying them during the retrieval process."
}

{
    "2024.findings-acl.139_s01": "The legal domain encompasses many specialized subfields (e.g., criminal law and civil law).",
    "2024.findings-acl.139_s02": "Similar to most previous research on legal case retrieval, our work focuses on Chinese criminal cases.",
    "2024.findings-acl.139_s03": "Besides, the proposed approaches require legal element annotations during training, which restricts their transferability to certain datasets."
}

{
    "2024.findings-acl.358_s01": "We did not conduct experiments on incomparable corpora.",
    "2024.findings-acl.358_s02": "Incomparable corpora across languages might have different domains, which results in significant differences in word ranks as Zipf‚Äö√Ñ√∂‚àö√ë‚àö¬•s law might be satisfied only for similar domains in practice.",
    "2024.findings-acl.358_s03": "This might limit the scope of our method.",
    "2024.findings-acl.358_s04": "However, multilingual models are commonly pretrained on comparable corpora, e.g., Wikipedia and CC."
}
